  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b000001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 1,
      "raw": "# iiXml\n",
      "level": 1,
      "title": "iiXml"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000002",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 6,
      "raw": "The independent `iiXmlMarkup` package exports `iiXml::Markup`: a C++23,\nQt-free source-preserving tag parser and HTML block range tracker used by\niiGeneralDocument. It does not depend on iiGeneralDocument or libxml2. See\n[the markup contract](docs/Markup.md).\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000004",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 7,
      "end_line": 7,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 8,
      "end_line": 12,
      "raw": "HTML block parsing, conversion, range tracking, serialization and editing are\nowned by iiXml as the optional Qt component `iiXml::HtmlBlock`. Existing\n`<iiHtmlBlock>` headers, the `iiHtmlBlock` namespace and the\n`iiHtmlBlock::iiHtmlBlock` CMake package remain compatibility interfaces.\nSee [HTML integration](docs/HtmlBlockIntegration.md).\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000006",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 13,
      "end_line": 13,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 14,
      "end_line": 17,
      "raw": "The C++23 Qt-free package `iiXmlNative` exports `iiXml::Native` and\n`<iiXml/Xml.h>` for bounded UTF-8 pull reading and XML writing. Configure with\n`-DIIXML_BUILD_QT_API=OFF` to avoid finding Qt. The existing QObject API remains\navailable independently. See [native contracts](docs/native.md).\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000008",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 18,
      "end_line": 18,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 19,
      "end_line": 19,
      "raw": "[Windows build and execution](docs/WindowsBuildAndRun.md)\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000010",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 20,
      "end_line": 20,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000011",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 21,
      "end_line": 23,
      "raw": "Package release: **0.1.1** (2026-10-19). This patch packages the current\nsource snapshot; build, test and installation evidence is recorded in the SDK\npatch-release report. Earlier versioned feature notes remain historical.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000012",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 24,
      "end_line": 25,
      "raw": "\n\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000013",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 26,
      "end_line": 26,
      "raw": "iiXml is a C++ library for defining custom XML rules and producing input/output that follows those rules.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000014",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 27,
      "end_line": 27,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000015",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 28,
      "end_line": 28,
      "raw": "Core parser element modules live under `Src/Elements/`. `OpenTag` tracks relaxed tag closure, while `ClosedTag` flags input that starts immediately with a `</tag>` closing marker before a matching opener appears in the same view.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000016",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 29,
      "end_line": 29,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000017",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 30,
      "end_line": 30,
      "raw": "## License\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "License"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000018",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 31,
      "end_line": 31,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000019",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 32,
