    },
    {
      "id": "b000027",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 40,
      "end_line": 40,
      "raw": "## File storage ownership\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "File storage ownership"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000028",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 41,
      "end_line": 41,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000029",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 42,
      "end_line": 49,
      "raw": "`FileParser` and `GetFile` accept an application-owned `iiXml::IO::FileReader`.\nThe XML library does not discover or link another SDK. The separate\n`example/FileProvider` consumer adapts iiFileProvider to that contract, retaining\nprovider-owned file reads and the existing file parsing checks. The default\nconstructor has no reader: path-based calls fail until a reader is supplied,\nwhile in-memory parsing is unchanged. Existing users must pass a reader and\nrebuild both the library and their application; object layout and behavior\nchanged. See [FileParser](docs/file_parser.md) and [GetFile](docs/get_file.md).\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000030",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 50,
      "end_line": 50,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
